abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.663\">vb.</abbr></b> be startled, alarmed (Targum <i>id.,</i> Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܘܗ</span>);—<i><abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.491\">Pe</abbr>.</i> <i><abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.500\">Pf.</abbr></i> 3 ms. ´<span class=\"hebrew\">ת</span>: <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan3:24\">Dn 3:24</a>.</p> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">7794,8450</span>]</abbr> † [<span class=\"hebrew\">תּוֺר</span>] <b>n.m.</b> bullock (Targum Syr.; BH <span class=\"hebrew\">שׁוֺר</span>, √ III. <span class=\"hebrew\">שׁור</span>);—<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> abs. <span class=\"hebrew\">תּוֺרִין</span>, for sacrifice <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:9\">Ezr 6:9</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:17\">6:17</a>; as eating grass <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:22\">Dn 4:22</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:29\">4:29</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:30\">4:30</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan5:21\">5:21</a>.</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8460,8478–79</span>]</abbr> † <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּחוֺת</span> <b>prep.</b> under (BH <span class=\"hebrew\">תַּחַתּ</span>; Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּחוֺת</span>, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܚܘܬ</span>, <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܚܝܬ</span>, adv. <span class=\"syriac\">ܠܬܚܬ</span>; Plam. <span class=\"hebrew\">מן לתחת</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.116\">Cooke<sup>320</sup></abbr>);—<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:27\">Dn 7:27</a> <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּחוֺת כָּל־שְׁמַיָּא</span> (cf. BH <b>II. 1</b>); in <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.380\">c.</abbr> sf. (as BH Syr. Targum) <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:9\">4:9</a> <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּחֹתֹהִי</span> (so Targum<sup>o</sup> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Lev15:10\">Lv 15:10</a>: <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.127\">Dalm</abbr>:§ 47, 2), v:<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:18\">18</a>. With <span class=\"hebrew\">מִן</span>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Jer10:11\">Je 10:11</a> <span class=\"hebrew\">מִן תְּחוֺת שְׁמַיָּא</span> (cf. BH <b>III. 2</b>); sf. <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan4:11\">Dn 4:11</a> <span class=\"hebrew\">מִן־תַּחְתּוֺהִי</span> (the form as Syr. adv. <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.622\">supr.</abbr>, unless a Hebraizing <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.521\">punct.</abbr>).</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">7950,8517</span>]</abbr> † <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלַג</span> <b>n.[m.]</b> snow (Targum Syr.; BH <span class=\"hebrew\">שֶׁלֶג</span>);—abs. ´<span class=\"hebrew\">ת</span>: <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:9\">Dn 7:9</a> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.589\">sim.</abbr>).</p></blockquote>",
