<b>n.m.,</b> <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלָתָה</span> <b>f.,</b> three (Targum Syr.; BH <span class=\"hebrew\">שׁ</span>.<span class=\"hebrew\">שָׁל</span>, <span class=\"hebrew\">שִׁלשָׁה</span>);—<b>m.</b> <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלָת</span> bef. <b>n.f.</b> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:5\">Dn 7:5</a>; n.f. om. v:<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:8\">8</a>, v:<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:20\">20</a>; <b>f.</b> <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלָתָה</span> bef. <b>n.m.</b> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan7:24\">7:24</a>; after, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan3:24\">3:24</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:3\">6:3</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:11\">6:11</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:14\">6:14</a>, so <span class=\"hebrew\">אָ֯</span> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:4\">Ezr 6:4</a>; <span class=\"hebrew\">יוֺם תְּלָתָה</span> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:15\">6:15</a> <i>third day;</i> sf. <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלָתֵּהוֺן</span> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.316\">K<sup>§</sup></abbr> 65, Anm,1) <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan3:23\">Dn 3:23</a> <i>the three of them.</i></p> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8531</span>]</abbr> † [<span class=\"hebrew\">תְלַּתּ</span>] <b>n.[m.]</b> a third part (so Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">תֻלְּ־תָ</span>, <span class=\"hebrew\">תַּלְתָּא</span>, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܘܠܬܐ</span>, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.436\">Nab.</abbr> <span class=\"hebrew\">תלת</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.558\">SAC<sup>121</sup></abbr>, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.454\">Ar.</abbr> <span class=\"arabic\">ثُلْثٌ</span>, <span class=\"arabic\">ثُلْثٌ</span>, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.17\">As.</abbr> <i>šulultu</i> (= <i>šuluštu</i>) <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.416\">Meissn<sup>Suppl</sup></abbr>. 95, cf. Dl<sup>WB</sup>; v. also <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.403\">M<sup>88</sup></abbr> * <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.160\">Dr</abbr>:<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan5:7\">Dn 5:7</a>);—emph. <span class=\"hebrew\">תַּלְתָּא</span> adv. <i>as one of three</i> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan5:16\">Dn 5:16</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan5:29\">5:29</a> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.59\">Bev</abbr> <i>the third day,</i> every three days, v. So in <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.403\">M<sup>88</sup></abbr> *).</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8523</span>]</abbr> ‡ † <span class=\"hebrew\">תַּלְתִּי</span> <b>adj. denom</b> (only BAram.) as <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.619\">subst.</abbr> third (ruler), i.e. <i>triumuir</i> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.403\">M<sup>89</sup></abbr>*), cf. foregoing, which possibly is abnormal form of same (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.316\">K<sup>§</sup></abbr> 65, 1, Anm.3), <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan5:7\">Dn 5:7</a>.</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8523</span>]</abbr> † [<span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלִיתַי</span>] <b>adj.</b> third (Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלִיתַי</span>, Syr.<span class=\"syriac\">ܬܠܝܬܝ</span>);—f. <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלִיתָיָא</span> <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.359\">Kt</abbr>, <span class=\"hebrew\">תָאָה</span>- <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.523\">Qr</abbr> (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.316\">K<sup>§</sup></abbr> 11, 1 b)) <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan2:39\">Dn 2:39</a> <i>the third kingdom</i>.</p></blockquote> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8533</span>]</abbr> † <span class=\"hebrew\">תְּלָתִין</span> <b>n.indecl.</b> thirty;—´<span class=\"hebrew\">יוֺמִין ת</span>: <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:8\">Dn 6:8</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:13\">6:13</a>.</p></blockquote>",
