 <b>adv.</b> there (so Eg. Aram. (<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.533\">RÉS<sup>361</sup></abbr> B 5 [also <span class=\"hebrew\">תנה</span>:A 4, so <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.108\">Cilic.</abbr>, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.116\">Cooke<sup>68</sup></abbr>. 5, cf. Palam. <span class=\"hebrew\">תנן</span> ib.:121. 3, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܢܢ</span>] S-C<sup>A</sup> 4, J 6); Targum <span class=\"hebrew\">תַּמָּן</span>, Syr. <span class=\"syriac\">ܬܡܢ</span>, v. BH <span class=\"hebrew\">שָׁם</span>);—<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra5:17\">Ezr 5:17</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:1\">6:1</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:12\">6:12</a>; ´<span class=\"hebrew\">מִן־ת</span>: <i>thence</i> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Ezra6:6\">6:6</a>.</p> <blockquote><p class=\"p\"><abbr>[Str<span class=\"strongs-number\">8540</span>]</abbr> † [<span class=\"hebrew\">תְּמַהּ</span>] <b>n.m.</b> wonder, as wrought by God (Targum Syr.; cf. BH [<span class=\"hebrew\">תָּמַהּ</span>]);—<abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> abs. <span class=\"hebrew\">תִּמְהִין</span> <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Dan6:28\">Dn 6:28</a>; emph. <span class=\"hebrew\">תִּמְהַיָּא</span> 3:32, <abbr data-bdb=\"ABBR.505\">pl.</abbr> sf. <span class=\"hebrew\">תִּמְה֫וֺהִי</span> v<sup>33</sup>.</p></blockquote>",
